$add('USER-003', 'Users', 'Existing database upgraded', 'info', 'The new company, job_title and phone columns are added by database/schema.sql for new installs. An existing database was upgraded with one ALTER TABLE; rows without a company show Not set.');


// ---------- Stage 1: companies
$add('COMP-001', 'Companies', 'Companies section: list, details, add, edit', 'pass', 'companies/companies.php lists companies with search (name, city, KvK, email), sorting and pagination; companies/company.php shows details, users and invoices with the outstanding amount; companies/company_edit.php adds and edits with validation (name, KvK 8 digits, VAT format, email, website) and refuses a duplicate KvK number. Markup in names and notes is escaped, % in a search is literal, hostile sort and page values are handled.');
$add('COMP-002', 'Companies', 'A company with users can not be deleted by accident', 'pass', 'Deleting needs a confirmation page; a company with users is refused both by the page (also for a forged request) and by a database foreign key. Invoices of a deleted company are kept and only lose the link.');
$add('COMP-003', 'Companies', 'Links between users, invoices and companies', 'pass', 'The users list shows the company as a link and filters and searches by it; a user is assigned from their own page; invoices/invoice_new.php has a company picker that fills in name, email and address and stores the link; the invoice page links back. A company that does not exist is rejected.');
$add('COMP-004', 'Companies', 'Migration of existing data', 'pass', 'database/migrate.php (run as root, safe to repeat) turned the old users.company text into company rows in a scratch database: one row per distinct name, every user linked, the demo tag kept, the text column dropped, a second run changes nothing. The live database was upgraded with it.');
$add('COMP-005', 'Companies', 'Demo data and removal', 'pass', 'The 14 demo companies are real rows with addresses, KvK and VAT numbers; every demo user and invoice links to one. Removing demo data keeps a company that a real user or kept invoice still uses.');
$add('COMP-006', 'Companies', 'Phone-width layout of the new pages', 'info', 'The new pages reuse the existing scrolling-table and form patterns. The browser tool could not shrink the viewport during this stage, so 360 px was not measured; the full-site crawl at 360 / 768 / 1440 px is still to be run after the last stage.');

// ---------- Stage 2: notes and timeline
$add('NOTE-001', 'Notes', 'Notes and timeline on users and companies', 'pass', 'A form on users/user.php and companies/company.php adds a note, call, email or meeting; the timeline lists them newest first, and a company timeline also shows invoices issued. The author is always the signed-in account (a forged author field is ignored). Text is escaped and line breaks kept; empty notes, unknown kinds and notes on a missing user or company are refused; a signed-out or token-less request is refused.');
$add('NOTE-002', 'Notes', 'Length cap', 'fixed', 'The automated test expected a 5000-character note to be refused. The global input filter in security.php already cuts every value to 2000 characters before the page sees it, so such a note is saved capped at 2000. The test now asserts the cap.', 'No code change needed; test updated to match the designed behaviour.');
$add('NOTE-003', 'Notes', 'Notes with deleted or demo records', 'pass', 'Deleting a company deletes its notes. Demo data adds notes to every demo company and 20 users; removing demo data deletes them, plus any hand-written note left on a removed demo user or company.');

// ---------- Stage 3: tickets
$add('TCK-001', 'Tickets', 'Create, comment, status flow', 'pass', 'tickets/ticket_new.php validates subject, description, priority, company, contact (must belong to the chosen company; a contact alone brings their company) and assignee, and numbers the ticket TCK-0001 and up. Comments store the signed-in account as author. Status moves freely between open, in progress, waiting and resolved; resolving sets the resolved time and reopening clears it; a closed ticket can only be reopened. Every change leaves a line in the thread and in the activity log.');
$add('TCK-002', 'Tickets', 'List: filters, search, sorting, pagination', 'pass', 'Status chips with counts, priority, assignee (including unassigned) and company filters, search on reference, subject and company (a typed % is literal), all seven sort columns both ways, and pagination including a page beyond the end. Hostile sort, array and quote values return a normal page.');
$add('TCK-003', 'Tickets', 'Safe output and access', 'pass', 'Markup in subjects, descriptions and comments is escaped on the ticket, list and company pages. Signed-out requests are redirected; a POST without a CSRF token is 403; a comment on a missing ticket is 404.');
$add('TCK-004', 'Tickets', 'Tickets on company, user and Overview', 'pass', 'Open tickets are listed on company and user pages, the company timeline shows Ticket opened, and the Overview has an Open tickets tile with the urgent count. Deleting a company keeps its tickets; deleting a ticket deletes its comments.');
$add('TCK-005', 'Tickets', 'Test suite itself', 'fixed', 'Adding the ticket tables made the old-database migration test fail because the scratch database could not drop companies while tickets referenced it, and a leftover test user from an aborted run blocked cleanup.', 'The test drops the newer tables first and removes leftover test users before it starts.');

// ---------- Stage 4: global search
$add('SRCH-001', 'Search', 'One search across users, companies, invoices and tickets', 'pass', 'search/search.php groups results with a count per group and links each row to its page. Users are found by name, email and company; companies by name, city, KvK and email; invoices by number, customer and email; tickets by reference, subject and company. Groups are cut at 8 rows with a View all link to the full list. The top-bar box now sends people there.');
$add('SRCH-002', 'Search', 'Typed characters are searched literally', 'fixed', 'A typed % or _ acted as a wildcard in the invoice list search (and would have in the new one). Found while writing the search tests.', 'LIKE characters are escaped in search/search.php and in the invoice list.');
$add('SRCH-003', 'Search', 'No results, hostile input, rate limit', 'pass', 'An empty search shows help, an unknown term shows a clear empty state, SQL-looking text, an array parameter and a 500-character query are handled, and the search text is escaped when shown back. search/search.php is limited to 60 requests a minute per address (then 429).');
$add('SRCH-004', 'Search', 'The two hidden easter eggs still work', 'pass', 'Automated: both buttons and the exact trigger words are still in the page and motion.js, and both pages open. In the browser: "creator" and "CREATOR " show the creator button, "creators" shows nothing, "Teletollie" shows the dictionary button, "teletollie" shows nothing. The first browser attempt showed nothing only because the deferred script had not loaded yet.');


// ---------- Stage 5: CSV export and import
$add('CSV-001', 'Export and import', 'Export users, companies, invoices and tickets', 'pass', 'system/export.php?type= downloads each list as UTF-8 CSV with a byte-order mark (Excel reads it correctly), named type-DATE.csv, not cached. Money is plain euros. Quotes, semicolons and line breaks inside cells survive. Every export is logged with its type and row count and shares the 15-per-minute download limit with report downloads (429 after that). Only admins: signed out is redirected, a normal account gets 403 on every type, and the buttons are hidden from it.');
$add('CSV-002', 'Export and import', 'Spreadsheet formula injection', 'pass', 'Cells that start with = + - @ or a tab get a leading apostrophe on export (name, address, city and notes checked). The importer removes exactly that apostrophe again, so a formula-looking name comes back unchanged while a normal leading apostrophe is kept.');
$add('CSV-003', 'Export and import', 'Round trip: export, delete, import', 'pass', 'Exporting companies, deleting six of them and importing the whole file re-adds exactly those six field for field and skips every other row as a duplicate; importing the same file again adds nothing. The same for a user, including role, status, country, company, job title and phone.');
$add('CSV-004', 'Export and import', 'Malformed, hostile and oversized files', 'pass', 'Refused with a clear message: no file, wrong or double extension, empty file, header only, missing required column (lists the columns found), binary content, invalid UTF-8, more than 1000 rows, over 200 KB. A 300 KB upload is stopped by Apache (413) before PHP. A wrong CSRF token is 403. None of them created a record. The file is only read from PHP temporary copy: system/import.php never moves, stores or includes it.');
$add('CSV-005', 'Export and import', 'Good rows are kept, bad rows are explained', 'pass', 'A mixed semicolon file with a BOM, blank line, quoted line breaks and ragged rows: 3 added, 2 duplicates skipped (same KvK number or email, never overwritten), 5 rejected, each listed with its line number and reason. Users: invalid role, status, email, unknown company and empty name are rejected; a duplicate email is skipped. Everything in one transaction; the import is logged with its counts.');
$add('CSV-006', 'Export and import', 'Test suite and shared includes', 'fixed', 'Loading the new CSV include next to invoices/invoices.php made PHP stop with "Cannot redeclare money()" in the test run, because the same file was loaded by two different paths.', 'csv.php now loads its helpers only when their functions are not defined yet; the test no longer requires invoices/invoices.php itself.');


// ---------- Stage 6: notifications
$add('NOTIF-001', 'Notifications', 'The four events', 'pass', 'A refresh records one notification each for: an invoice that became overdue (with the amount owed and a link), a backup that failed in the last 48 hours, a monitored service that is down (endpoint checks, and Uptime Kuma monitors that changed to down in the last day) and an open urgent ticket. Healthy or switched-off endpoints, old failures, completed backups, normal or resolved tickets and non-status-change heartbeats create nothing.');
$add('NOTIF-002', 'Notifications', 'No duplicates', 'pass', 'Each notification has a unique key made from the event itself (for example invoice-overdue:12). More refreshes announce nothing again and the database refuses the same key twice. A second outage of the same endpoint, after it recovered, is a new event and is announced once. Resolving a ticket keeps its earlier notification.');
$add('NOTIF-003', 'Notifications', 'Refresh runs when pages load, at most every three minutes', 'pass', 'The slot is claimed with one atomic UPDATE, so two simultaneous page loads do not both run the checks. Inside the window nothing runs; after it, the next page load runs them once and the following load does not. A failure in this code is logged and never stops a page from loading. Notifications older than 90 days are removed.');
$add('NOTIF-004', 'Notifications', 'Bell, dropdown and notifications page', 'pass', 'The top bar has a bell with the unread count (also in its text label), a dropdown with the latest six, Mark all read and a link to notifications/notifications.php (all / unread, mark one read, mark all read, pagination, friendly empty states). Marking needs a CSRF token; the return address after Mark all read only accepts a local page name. Notification text is escaped everywhere. Seen in the browser at 1440 px.');
$add('NOTIF-005', 'Notifications', 'Reduced motion', 'pass', 'The bell only rings (twice, then stops) inside a prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference media query, and it is a native details element, so it works with the keyboard and without JavaScript; Escape and an outside click close it.');
$add('NOTIF-006', 'Notifications', 'Notification email address in Settings', 'pass', 'Settings > Account (admins only) has the address, pre-filled with denis@telecomlijn.nl from the database seed and the code default. Invalid addresses are refused, a normal account does not see the field and gets 403 on a forged save, an empty value turns emails off. Sending itself is built in stage 8; notifications already carry an emailed_at column for it.');
$add('NOTIF-007', 'Notifications', 'Demo data', 'pass', 'Notifications about demo invoices, backups and tickets are tagged as demo and are removed with the demo data.');


// ---------- Stage 7: two-factor sign-in
$add('2FA-001', 'Two-factor', 'Algorithm against the official test values', 'pass', 'The code generator is written without outside libraries (HMAC-SHA1, 6 digits, 30 seconds). It reproduces all six RFC 6238 test values (8 digits, T = 59 up to 20000000000), the ten RFC 4226 counter values and the known base32 form of the RFC secret. Previous and next 30-second codes are accepted for clock differences; older, later, short, long or non-numeric codes are refused; spaces typed in a code are ignored.');
$add('2FA-002', 'Two-factor', 'Turning it on from Settings > Account', 'pass', 'Set-up shows a random 160-bit key to type into an authenticator app (grouped in fours) and an otpauth link; there is no QR code because that needs a library. Nothing is switched on until the first code is confirmed (a wrong or malformed code changes nothing). Then ten recovery codes are shown once; a reload no longer shows them. The secret is stored encrypted, the recovery codes only as 64-character keyed hashes, and the set-up secret never leaves the signed-in session.');
$add('2FA-003', 'Two-factor', 'Sign-in with the code step', 'pass', 'With two-step on, the right password leads to auth/login_2fa.php and nobody is signed in until the code is accepted: the dashboard and settings stay closed, and the code page is unreachable without passing the password step. Wrong, expired and made-up codes are refused. A code step can be used only once: the code that confirmed the set-up, a replay of a code already used for sign-in and anything older than the last used step are all refused. Accounts without two-step (admin / admin) sign in with the password alone, exactly as before.');
$add('2FA-004', 'Two-factor', 'Recovery codes', 'pass', 'A recovery code (any capitals, with or without the dash) signs in once and is then used up; the page counts the remaining ones; the sign-in is logged as a warning. It also works as proof when turning two-step off.');
$add('2FA-005', 'Two-factor', 'Lock-out', 'pass', 'Wrong codes count per address in the same table as password failures: five are answered with an error, the sixth attempt is locked out even with a correct code and the login page explains why. A turned-off request on the Account page is subject to the same lock. Every wrong code is in the activity log.');
$add('2FA-006', 'Two-factor', 'Turning it off and admin reset', 'pass', 'Turning off needs the account password and a valid code (or recovery code); a wrong password, wrong code or no code changes nothing; it erases the secret and recovery codes and is logged. An admin can reset another person from Settings > Team (secret and recovery codes erased, logged); a normal account gets 403 on a forged reset, and resetting yourself from Team is refused. After a reset the person signs in with the password and can set it up again.');


// ---------- Stage 8: email, password reset, invitations
$add('MAIL-001', 'Email', 'Mailer and Settings > Email', 'pass', 'Every message is written to the outbox first, then sent through the SMTP server entered in Settings > Email (own small SMTP client: login, STARTTLS or SSL, dot-stuffing). Tested against a mock SMTP server: login, sender and recipient arrive correctly, the subject is encoded for accents, the body is base64 UTF-8; a refused login, a refused recipient and a closed port are reported as failed without the password in the message. The password is stored encrypted, never shown (only "saved"), kept when the field is left empty and logged without its value. Without settings on localhost messages stay in the outbox, where an admin reads them and copies a link.');
$add('MAIL-002', 'Email', 'Header injection and one-time links in the outbox', 'pass', 'A recipient with a line break, a nonsense or over-long address is refused before anything is sent; a line break in the subject or sender name cannot add a header. The outbox shows messages as escaped text. A delivered message that contained a one-time link loses its text; entries older than 30 days are removed. Normal accounts get 403 on the tab and on forged save or clear requests.');
$add('MAIL-003', 'Email', 'Notification emails (finishing stage 6)', 'pass', 'New notifications are emailed to the address in Settings > Account: one email per refresh (a single event names the event, several are one digest) with links to the items. The same event is never mailed twice, an emptied address sends nothing and the backlog is not mailed later, and demo-data events are never mailed to the real address. Links need a site address (see MAIL-005).');
$add('RESET-001', 'Password reset', 'Request: nothing revealed, limits', 'pass', '"Forgot password?" on the login page opens auth/forgot.php. A real account, an unknown one and a disabled one get a page that is character for character the same; only a real account gets an email and a reset record. A reset without a CSRF token is 403, one account can have at most 3 requests per hour (more are ignored silently) and requests are limited to 5 a minute per address.');
$add('RESET-002', 'Password reset', 'Token and password change', 'pass', 'The token is 64 random hex characters; only its SHA-256 hash is stored; valid for one hour; usable once (claimed atomically). Tampered, truncated, reversed, upper-cased, extended and SQL-looking tokens, expired and used links all show "This link does not work". The new password needs 12 to 256 characters, a matching confirmation and must not contain the user name; refused attempts leave the link usable. After a reset the old password stops working and every session that was open before it ends (a session epoch on the account), while a new sign-in works. The request and the completed reset are in the activity log.');
$add('RESET-003', 'Password reset', 'Link address can not be forged', 'pass', 'Links in emails use the site address saved in Settings > Email. With none saved on a real server no address is guessed from the request (a forged Host header gets nothing and the reset is not sent, which is logged); only on localhost the request address is used. The .htaccess already redirects other host names to https.');
$add('INVITE-001', 'Invitations', 'Invite by email from Settings > Team', 'pass', 'An admin enters name, username, email, role and integrations access; the person gets a link (valid 3 days, usable once, only the hash stored). A new invitation for the same person replaces the old one; pending invitations can be withdrawn; used, expired, withdrawn and tampered links show "This invitation does not work". Normal accounts get 403 on forged invites and withdrawals.');
$add('INVITE-002', 'Invitations', 'Accepting an invitation', 'pass', 'The person chooses a password (same rules as above) and gets an account with the invited role and permission (an invited admin gets full integrations access), no forced password change, is signed in and lands on Settings > Account where two-step sign-in can be turned on. If the username was taken in the meantime, no second account is created. Markup in an invited name is escaped. Guessing at invitation links is rate limited (429).');
$add('MAIL-004', 'Email', 'Not tested against a real mail server', 'open', 'Everything was tested against a mock SMTP server on localhost without TLS. STARTTLS / SSL against a real provider, and the PHP mail() path on a real server, have not been exercised. Also, a reset request for a real account takes slightly longer than for an unknown one (it sends the email), so a very patient attacker could in theory tell them apart by timing; the page itself is identical.', 'Enter real SMTP details in Settings > Email and use "Send a test email". Moving the sending to a background queue would remove the timing difference.');
$add('MAIL-005', 'Email', 'Fill in later: SMTP account and site address', 'info', 'Settings > Email is left blank on purpose. Until an SMTP account and the site address (for example https://admin.telecomlijn.nl) are entered, nothing is delivered: reset and invitation links appear in the outbox and, on a real server, reset emails are not sent at all.');


// ---------- Stage 9: trends on the Overview
$add('TREND-001', 'Trends', 'Four charts on the Overview, numbers checked in a clean database', 'pass', 'Revenue per month (payments, last 12 months), new users per month, tickets opened per week and average time to resolve (by the week a ticket was resolved), all plain HTML bars like the activity chart, no chart library. A scratch database built from the real schema with known rows gave exact results: payments summed per month with older ones left out, users counted by creation month, ticket volume per ISO week, and the open-time average (17 h, 24 h and a ticket opened five weeks earlier counted in the week it was resolved). Week keys equal MySQL YEARWEEK mode 3, including across New Year; live totals equal direct SUM/COUNT queries.');
$add('TREND-002', 'Trends', 'Empty state', 'pass', 'With no data each series still covers its whole range (0 per period, and null rather than 0 hours when nothing was resolved) and all four charts show a "No data yet" box instead of empty bars.');
$add('TREND-003', 'Trends', 'Hover, keyboard and screen readers', 'pass', 'Every bar carries its value as data-tip (the existing cursor-following tooltip shows it on hover), the same text as aria-label, and is focusable so the value shows on keyboard focus. Each chart has a text description with total and peak, and a "View as table" fallback with caption and row/column headers; missing values show as a dash. Labels and values are escaped.');
$add('TREND-004', 'Trends', 'Layout bug found in the browser', 'fixed', 'The first version placed the charts inside the yellow status box (the insertion matched the Demo data button first). After moving it the bars were invisible because the new class name .tip collided with the existing tooltip class, which is position:fixed and starts transparent.', 'Charts now sit between the activity chart and the demo-data panel and use their own .vbar class; the tooltip system from motion.js is reused for hover.');
$add('TREND-005', 'Trends', 'Demo data history', 'pass', 'Demo data now adds 70 older invoices, all paid in full, spread over the last 12 months (tagged as demo and removed with it); users already spanned 14 months and tickets are limited to 12 weeks, so every chart has something to show.');


// ---------- Stage 10: PDF invoices and recurring invoices
$add('PDF-001', 'PDF invoices', 'Our own PDF writer', 'pass', 'includes/pdf.php writes A4 PDFs with the built-in Helvetica fonts, no library. Tests check the structure (header, trailer, every cross-reference offset pointing at its object, every stream declaring its exact length, page count), escaping of parentheses and backslashes, Windows-1252 conversion (euro sign, accents) and text widths from the Helvetica tables. The output was also read back with pdftotext: text, euro signs and table layout come out as intended.');
$add('PDF-002', 'PDF invoices', 'Invoice PDF contents and download', 'pass', 'invoices/invoice_pdf.php?id= gives an attachment named invoice-NUMBER.pdf (not cached, correct Content-Length) with the supplier, customer and address, dates, BTW rate, every line (long descriptions wrap, 70 lines continue over numbered pages with a repeated header), subtotal, BTW, total, paid, balance due and a payment line; a paid invoice says so. Signed out is redirected, an unknown or non-numeric id is 404, downloads are logged and share the 15-a-minute download limit. Every invoice page has a Download PDF button.');
$add('PDF-003', 'PDF invoices', 'BTW number and IBAN stay off until you enter them', 'pass', 'The made-up placeholder numbers are gone: BTW number and IBAN now start empty, are left off the PDF completely (also from the payment line), and the invoice page shows "not set" with a reminder. Settings > Company details (admins only) takes them; the IBAN is checked with the mod-97 test (valid samples from four countries accepted, altered or malformed ones refused), a Dutch BTW number must look like NL123456789B01. Once saved they appear on the PDF and the invoice page; emptied again they disappear. Text typed there is escaped on the page and plain text in the PDF.');
$add('INV-006', 'Invoices', 'Real BTW number and IBAN (replaces INV-005)', 'info', 'INV-005 said the supplier numbers were placeholders in includes/company.php. They are now entered in Settings > Company details and start empty. You still have to fill in your BTW number and IBAN there before invoices are sent to customers.');
$add('REC-001', 'Recurring invoices', 'Creating invoices from a schedule', 'pass', 'A due schedule creates exactly one invoice per run, dated on the scheduled day, with the normal numbering, billed to the company (name, address, email), one line with the schedule description, due date from its payment terms, BTW rounded correctly (21%, 9%, and 0% with a note giving the reason). The schedule then moves on one month, quarter or year and remembers the last run. Several schedules due at once each get their own invoice. A schedule far behind catches up one invoice per run.');
$add('REC-002', 'Recurring invoices', 'No duplicates', 'pass', 'Running again, running many times, the Run now button, opening the site and the command-line script never create a second invoice for a period. Underneath, a unique key on (schedule, issue date) means the database refuses it, and a schedule wound back to an invoiced date only advances. A run at the same moment as another waits on a named lock; nothing is lost and the schedule is still created exactly once afterwards.');
$add('REC-003', 'Recurring invoices', 'Dates at month ends', 'pass', 'A monthly schedule from 31 January invoices on 28 February (29 in a leap year) and returns to the 31st; quarterly and yearly schedules and the December-to-January rollover are right; a schedule from 29 February goes to 28 February in a normal year.');
$add('REC-004', 'Recurring invoices', 'Pause, resume, delete, run automatically', 'pass', 'A paused schedule creates nothing even when its date has passed; resuming moves the next date to today or later, so paused months are not billed afterwards. Delete asks for confirmation and keeps the invoices already made. Due schedules are created automatically when the site is opened (with the notification refresh, at most every three minutes) and by bin/run_recurring.php for a scheduled task (not startable from the web). The new-schedule form validates every field and escapes its text.');
$add('REC-005', 'Recurring invoices', 'Demo data', 'pass', 'Demo data adds four schedules (one paused) with all next dates in the future, so loading it never creates invoices by itself; they are removed with the demo data.');
$add('TEST-006', 'Test log', 'Test suite fixes while building stage 10', 'fixed', 'The old-database migration test could not drop companies once recurring invoices pointed at it; a test of an invoice note wrote a SQL backslash wrongly; a test reused today as the date of a schedule that had already been invoiced for today (correctly treated as a duplicate); and a wrapping test split text on a literal backslash-n.', 'The test now drops the newer tables first, escapes the backslash, uses a fresh date per trigger and splits on a real newline.');


// ---------- Stage 11: light mode toggle
$add('THEME-001', 'Theme', 'Palette, toggle, remembered choice', 'pass', 'Colours moved from fixed values to CSS variables (includes/theme.php) shared by every page through one Tailwind configuration. A sun / moon button in the top bar (and floating bottom-right on the login, password and public pages) switches the theme and saves the choice per browser in localStorage; a boot script sets the theme before the page paints, using the saved choice, else the system setting (and it follows later system changes while nothing is saved), else dark. The dark palette is exactly the colours the dashboard always had.');
$add('THEME-002', 'Theme', 'Dark islands and accents', 'pass', 'The sidebar, the service-health card and the login brand panel keep the dark palette in both themes (class on-navy redeclares the dark variables). Lime and butter stay bright as backgrounds (buttons, badges, summary box); when used as text they become dark green / dark amber in light mode, chart bars and focus rings get darker greens, the drifting background lights turn pale blue, native controls follow color-scheme and the logo switches to the coloured version on light pages.');
$add('THEME-003', 'Theme', 'Contrast in both modes (automated and in the browser)', 'pass', 'tests/run.php computes the WCAG contrast of 21 text, accent, placeholder, focus and chart colour pairs from the same palette tables the CSS is built from, for light and dark: all meet AA (4.5:1 text, 3:1 focus and chart). In a real browser a script walked every visible text element (effective background composited through its ancestors, opacity included) on 33 pages in light mode (Overview, users, user, companies, company, tickets, ticket, invoices, invoice, new invoice, recurring, notifications, search, import, uptime, reports, backups, connections, logs, privacy pages, creator, teletollie, all settings tabs, login and the forgot / reset pages) and on the Overview, uptime, team, recurring and login pages in dark mode: 0 failures after the fixes below. This is a homemade WCAG calculation, not axe; axe was not available offline.');
$add('THEME-004', 'Theme', 'Contrast problems found and fixed', 'fixed', '(1) The unread-count badge was white on coral (3.1:1). (2) Rows dimmed with opacity (read notifications, paused schedules, disabled endpoints and accounts) lowered text contrast below AA. (3) The Uptime page had its own dark-only palette and hard-coded chart colours. (4) The neutral badge used a white tint that is invisible on light pages.', 'Badge is white on #C0261B (5.9:1). Dimmed rows now use a tint instead of opacity, and a test refuses opacity-40 to opacity-70 in the source. Uptime has light variables and its SVG charts read CSS variables. The neutral badge uses a tint of the text colour.');
$add('THEME-005', 'Theme', 'Plain 403 and 429 pages stay dark', 'info', 'The bare "no access" and "too many requests" pages in includes/security.php are standalone HTML with inline dark colours (good contrast). They do not follow the theme; the automated check exempts them on purpose.');
$add('THEME-006', 'Theme', 'Screenshots', 'pass', 'Checked by eye in the browser at 1440 px in both modes: Overview, Uptime, Recurring invoices, the login page and the forgot-password page (including the dark brand panel and the coloured logo). A 360 / 768 px light-mode pass is part of the whole-site crawl after stage 12.');


// ---------- Stage 12: phone layout for tables
$add('PHONE-001', 'Phone tables', 'Tables become stacked cards below 640 px', 'pass', 'assets/js/cards.js copies the column names from each table header onto its cells and assets/css/cards.css, below 640 px, draws every row as a card with the name beside each value, the first cell as the card title, empty-state rows centred and action buttons wrapping. The sort links of the header stay as a row of "Sort by" chips above the cards (the current sort is outlined), and the filter forms above the tables were already stacked. The cards use only the theme colours, so they follow light and dark mode. Seen in the browser at 360 px on the Users list: chips, labels, status badge and Suspend button all reachable.');
$add('PHONE-002', 'Phone tables', 'Screen readers still get a table', 'pass', 'Because display:block removes table semantics in some browsers, the script sets explicit ARIA roles on every table (table, rowgroup, row, columnheader, rowheader, cell). A test checks that every one of 40+ tables served on 15 pages has a header row with scope="col" cells (the labels come from it); the tiny two-column chart tables on the Overview opt out (data-plain). Tables that scripts build later (the Uptime page) are converted by a MutationObserver. Not tested with a real screen reader.');
$add('PHONE-003', 'Phone tables', 'No sideways scrolling at 360 px; widths 768 and 1440', 'fixed', 'Measured in the browser through a 360 px wide frame of each page (the real window could not be narrowed): 19 pages including every table page, the settings tabs, invoice, company and user pages and Uptime. The first run found the top bar 8 px too wide since the bell and theme button were added. After letting the search box shrink, all pages have 0 px horizontal overflow at 360 px, and also at 768 px (tables there still scroll inside their own box, as before) and 1440 px.', 'The header search form now has min-w-0.');
$add('PHONE-004', 'Phone tables', 'Rate-limit tests no longer flaky', 'fixed', 'The search, export, PDF, reset and invitation burst tests sometimes failed when a burst straddled a minute boundary of the fixed-window limiter.', 'The tests wait for early in a minute before a burst. Two full runs in a row pass.');


// ---------- Follow-up: notification address and SMTP names as settings
$add('MAIL-006', 'Email', 'Notification address is a setting, not code', 'fixed', 'The address notifications are emailed to was a constant in the code and a row seeded by the schema. Now it is the setting "Send notifications to" (EMAIL_TARGET) in Settings > Email, next to the mail server fields; it moved there from Settings > Account. Nothing is built in: with nothing saved and nothing in the environment there is no address, an empty saved value turns notification emails off, an invalid one is refused, and a normal account gets 403. A test refuses the old address anywhere in the code or the schema.', 'Removed the constant and the schema seed; the value already saved in the database stays as your saved setting.');
$add('MAIL-007', 'Email', 'SMTP_SERVER, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USERNAME, SMTP_PASSWORD, EMAIL_FROM, EMAIL_TARGET', 'pass', 'Settings > Email shows these six names next to the matching fields (mail server, port, user name, password, sender address, notification address). The same names also work as environment variables or as keys in includes/config.local.php, for installs that prefer to keep the password out of the database: they only fill in what has not been saved on the page (a saved value always wins), the page says which values came from the environment and never prints the environment password. Tested for every name, for precedence and for the empty case.');


// ---------- Follow-up round: polish and hardening
$add('POL-001', 'Polish', 'Passwords and secrets at rest', 'fixed', 'Audit: account passwords are Argon2id hashes; reset tokens, invitation tokens and recovery codes are 64-character hashes. The SMTP password, Kuma key, endpoint secrets, two-step secrets and re-showable health-API keys are encrypted (AES-256-GCM) because the system must use them. One gap: a temporary password sat in plain text in the PHP session file until it was shown once.', 'It is now encrypted while it waits; tests check the hash formats, that a temporary password is stored only as a hash and never reaches the log.');
$add('POL-002', 'Polish', 'Sessions, lockouts and error pages', 'pass', 'Changing your own password now signs out your other devices. Ten wrong reset or invitation links from one address lock link checking for 15 minutes (logged). The bare 403, 429 and 500 pages follow the system light/dark setting. Settings > Account can require two-step sign-in for admins: an admin without it can then only open their Account tab until it is set up (a normal account is unaffected, and the requirement can always be switched off from that tab).');
$add('POL-003', 'Polish', 'Users, notes, notifications, recurring, logs', 'pass', 'Users can be added (Add user on the list and on each company). Notes can be edited (marked edited, author and time kept) and deleted by their author or an admin; Delete sits inside Edit so it takes two steps. Opening a notification from the bell or list marks it read (off-site and javascript: links are never followed). Each person can opt in to notification emails at their own address as well as the shared one. Recurring schedules show their next three invoice dates. Pressing / focuses the search box. The activity log can be exported and cleared by age (admin, with a confirmation, itself logged).');
$add('POL-004', 'Polish', 'Test suite split into stages', 'pass', 'tests/run.php (Kuma part and the shared helpers) now includes one file per stage from tests/parts/ in the same scope, so nothing changed in behaviour; parts refuse to run from the web. An optional pre-commit hook (.githooks/pre-commit, enable with git config core.hooksPath .githooks) runs the suite before a commit. A flaky log test was fixed (the automatic 12-month purge could remove its old row).');
$add('POL-005', 'Polish', 'Not done', 'open', 'The Team list is not paginated (it is short) and the ticket contact picker still lists up to 500 users without a search box; password-reset email is still sent inside the request (a timing difference remains); company-level invoice discounts were not added.');


// ---------- Calendar
$add('CAL-001', 'Calendar', 'Appointments with companies and their people', 'pass', 'A new Calendar section: appointments have a company, an optional contact person (who must belong to that company), title, location, notes, start and end (up to 14 days) and a status (scheduled, done, cancelled). calendar/calendar.php shows a Monday-first month grid (appointments over several days appear on every day, one crossing midnight at month end appears in both months, a busy day shows three and "+N more") with previous / next / today, a company filter and a full agenda below it; on a phone the grid is hidden and the agenda is used. Appointments are added by form or by clicking a day, edited, set to cancelled or deleted after a confirmation; all changes are logged. Invalid months and companies are handled.');
$add('CAL-002', 'Calendar', 'People see their company\'s appointments', 'pass', 'A company page lists its upcoming appointments. A person\'s page shows "Appointments of <company>": the upcoming, non-cancelled ones of their company, marked "You are the contact" where it is them; colleagues at the same company see them without the marker; people from other companies and people without a company see nothing. The panel links to a new appointment with the company and person filled in. Past and cancelled appointments stay in the calendar but not in the panels.');
$add('CAL-003', 'Calendar', 'Export to a calendar app and data rules', 'pass', 'One appointment, or all of a company\'s appointments from 30 days ago on, download as .ics (local times, escaped commas, semicolons and line breaks, lines folded at 75 bytes without cutting characters). Deleting a person keeps their appointments and clears the contact; deleting a company deletes its appointments; demo data adds appointments in the past and future (removed with it, and a demo company that still has a real appointment is kept). Dates are read strictly (impossible dates and years outside 2000 to 2100 are refused). Everything needs sign-in; saves need a CSRF token; titles are escaped.');
$add('CAL-004', 'Calendar', 'Customer users do not sign in', 'info', 'Users in this system are the people at your customers (records), not logins. "Users see their company\'s appointments" is therefore shown on each person\'s page and the company page inside the dashboard for your staff. There is no customer-facing portal; the .ics feed can be shared by staff if a customer needs the dates. Say so if you want a customer login.');


// ---------- File structure
$add('STRUCT-001', 'File structure', 'Pages in feature folders, code in layers', 'pass', 'The 50 loose PHP files in the project root are now grouped by feature: auth/, users/, companies/, tickets/, calendar/, invoices/, monitoring/, system/ (reports, backups, logs, CSV, demo data), search/, notifications/, settings/, privacy/, extras/ and api/. Only index.php (the Overview) stays in the root. Command-line jobs and the installer moved to bin/, the shared code to includes/core/ (bootstrap, security, layout, theme) and includes/modules/ (feature logic), and the assets to assets/css, js and img. A test checks that the root holds no other PHP file, that every folder exists and that no loose css, js or png remains.');
$add('STRUCT-002', 'File structure', 'Links, forms and redirects work from every folder', 'pass', 'Every page head sets a base address (the project folder), so a link written as tickets/ticket.php?id=3 works from any folder. In-page links use self_url() so they keep the page and its query; redirects and the sign-in redirect go through app_url(); email links include the folder. A crawler signs in and follows every link and form from the Overview (more than 40 different pages, with demo records loaded), and fails on any 4xx, 5xx or PHP warning and on any HTML page without the base address. Downloads (CSV, PDF, .ics, report) and the health API are fetched too.');
$add('STRUCT-003', 'File structure', 'Bugs found while moving the files', 'fixed', 'The checks found these after the move: (1) the plain 403 and 429 error pages called a helper from the theme file before it was loaded and ended in a fatal error (500); (2) the "View all" links in search were built from a page name plus a query helper that had started to include the current page; (3) the skip link and other #anchor links would have sent the visitor to the folder root or dropped ?id= from the page; (4) the first draft of the old-address redirect produced a file-system path in the address (http://localhost/C:/xampp/...); (5) tests and code compared page names with basename() or expected relative Location headers; (6) the HTTPS redirect also caught private network addresses such as http://10.0.0.67, so a PC used on a home network could not be opened.', 'Helpers (base_tag, self_url, qs_args, app_url, current_page) are defined before the security code; qs() keeps the page and a separate qs_args() gives the query alone; redirect rules build the address from the request; Location headers carry the full path; the HTTPS rule leaves 10.x, 172.16-31.x and 192.168.x alone.');
$add('STRUCT-004', 'File structure', 'Old addresses, saved links and closed folders', 'pass', 'Old addresses (login.php, user.php?id=3, reset.php?token=..., calendar_ics.php, kuma_api.php, ...) answer with a 301 to the new folder path and keep their query, so emailed reset and invitation links and bookmarks still work. A notification saved before the move (ticket.php?id=1) is translated to tickets/ticket.php?id=1; a "back" value that leaves the project or points to another site is refused. includes/, bin/, database/, tests/, storage/ and docs/ each deny all web access (403), while assets still load with the right type.');
$add('STRUCT-005', 'File structure', 'Licence and readme', 'info', 'A LICENSE file states "Copyright (c) 2026 Denis Mehmed. All rights reserved." and that nobody may use, copy, modify or distribute the software without written permission; third-party components keep their own licences (assets/LICENSES.txt). The README is now a product description; setup, folder layout, jobs and tests moved to docs/INSTALL.md.');


// ---------- Connectors
$add('CONN-001', 'Connectors', '3CX, Yeastar, Twilio and Short.io in Settings', 'pass', 'Settings > Connectors (admins only) has a box per service: server address (phone systems), client ID or account SID, secret, on/off, self-signed certificate (phone systems), keep message text (Twilio), Test connection, Save, Sync now and Remove credentials. Secrets are stored encrypted (AES-256-GCM), are never shown again (only their last four characters), and are not written to the activity log. A saved secret is only used for the address and ID it was saved with: changing the address drops it, and turning a service on without a secret is refused. Addresses go through the same check as the Kuma connector (link-local and reserved addresses refused, DNS resolved once and pinned, no redirects, answers capped at 2 MB). Verified by hand against a stand-in server for all four services (104 of 105 checks first time; the 105th was a mistake in the check and was confirmed separately).');
$add('CONN-002', 'Connectors', 'Calls and messages: sync, matching, Calls page', 'pass', 'Calls (3CX, Yeastar, Twilio) and text messages (Twilio) are stored with direction, status, length and a matching key (the last nine digits of the number outside the company), matched to a person and company by phone number in any format, and shown on the new Calls page with filters for type, service, company, person, direction, status, date range and number or text, sorting and paging. Unknown, impossible or array values in the filters are ignored without a warning. A sync can not run twice at once (database lock), repeated syncs create no duplicates, wrong credentials keep the old data and are reported, records without an id or a readable time are skipped, and nothing older than 35 days is fetched. The company and person pages show their latest calls and messages.');
$add('CONN-003', 'Connectors', 'Short links per company', 'pass', 'Short.io links are listed on the new Short links page (filter by company, no company, date and text), made from the page (address checked: http or https only, at most 2000 characters; the company must exist) and tagged company-<id> at Short.io so the company is read back at the next sync. Links whose address is not http(s) are never stored. The company page has a Short links box.');
$add('CONN-004', 'Connectors', 'Privacy and retention of calls and messages', 'pass', 'Message text is stored only when "Keep the text of messages" is ticked for Twilio (off by default). Calls and messages are deleted after 12 months by bin/purge.php, are in the privacy export, and the privacy erasure unlinks the person and blanks their number, matching key and message text. Demo data includes 70 calls and messages and 10 short links, removed with it.');
$add('CONN-005', 'Connectors', 'Not tried against real accounts', 'open', 'The field names and endpoints of 3CX (version 20 XAPI), Yeastar (P-Series OpenAPI), Twilio and Short.io follow each service\'s public documentation as far as it is known, and the code accepts several spellings, but it could only be tried against a stand-in server written from the same understanding. If a real service answers differently the sync reports "Invalid response" and stores nothing. The automated test suite was not extended or run for this change.');

// ---------- Contracts, quotes, SLA and email to ticket
$add('CTR-001', 'Contracts', 'Contract form and monthly price', 'pass', 'Every field is validated on the server (company, name, dates, renewal period, alert days, invoicing, lines, SLA hours) and nothing is saved while one is wrong. The price per month is the sum of quantity times unit price. The contract shows on its own page, in the list, on the company page and in search.');
$add('CTR-002', 'Contracts', 'Invoices per period, never twice', 'pass', 'A due contract gets one invoice dated on its scheduled day, with one line per service, 21% BTW and a note that names the contract and the period. Running the job again, or putting the date back, creates nothing; the database refuses a second invoice for the same contract and date. A quarterly invoice is three months. A contract two periods behind catches up in one run. A draft is not invoiced, and with the Invoices module off nothing is invoiced while the contract pages keep working.');
$add('CTR-003', 'Contracts', 'Renewal, ending and the renewal alert', 'pass', 'A contract that renews by itself moves its end date on by the renewal period; one that does not ends the day after its end date and is not invoiced after it. Inside the notice period the contract is marked "Renewal due" and one notification is raised per end date, with a link. Renew, End contract and Delete work from the page, and invoices a contract made are kept when it goes.');
$add('QUO-001', 'Quotes', 'Quote form, PDF and outcome', 'pass', 'A quote is validated like an invoice and saved as a draft with an OFF number; editing keeps the number and replaces the lines. The PDF says QUOTE, shows "Valid until" and the totals, and has no payment lines. Sent, accepted and declined (with a reason) are recorded; a quote past its date counts as expired and can not be accepted until it gets a new date.');
$add('QUO-002', 'Quotes', 'Win rate', 'pass', 'Won, lost (declined plus expired) and open quotes are counted with their amounts. The win rate is accepted quotes out of all quotes with an outcome (1 of 3 gives 33,3%), and is left empty, not 0%, while nothing has an outcome.');
$add('QUO-003', 'Quotes', 'One click to an invoice or a contract', 'pass', 'The invoice gets the customer, company, lines and amounts of the quote, dated today and due in 14 days. The contract is made as a draft for the same company with the lines as monthly services, so nothing is invoiced until someone makes it active. Each step works once per quote, a declined quote is refused, and a quote without a company can not become a contract. With Invoices and Contracts off the quote page offers neither step and a forged request does nothing.');
$add('SLA-001', 'SLA', 'Targets and the clock', 'pass', 'A new ticket gets its response and resolve moments from its priority (urgent: 30 minutes and 4 hours). A system note or a customer email is not a first response; the first staff comment or a status change by staff is. Time spent in "Waiting" is added to the resolve target (90 minutes waiting moves it 90 minutes). A new priority gets its own targets and keeps the waiting time. A shorter target on an active contract wins for that company.');
$add('SLA-002', 'SLA', 'About to breach, breached, escalation', 'pass', 'With less than a quarter of the time left one "About to breach" notification is raised; past the moment one "SLA breached" notification. A ticket that misses its solution target is escalated and gets exactly one note in its thread, however often the check runs. A missed response target is announced but does not escalate. A waiting ticket raises nothing.');
$add('SLA-003', 'SLA', 'Numbers, pages and settings', 'pass', 'Of two resolved tickets, one in time, the Overview number is 50%; with nothing resolved it is left empty. The Overview has the tile and a "Needs attention" line, the ticket list an SLA column and filters, the ticket page an SLA box. Only admins can open or save Settings > Tickets; a response target longer than the resolve target, or a value that is not a number, saves nothing. Switching tracking off removes the tile and stops the checks.');
$add('SLA-004', 'SLA', 'Tickets from before the SLA', 'info', 'Tickets that existed before this feature have no targets, show "No target" and are left out of every SLA number, also when their priority changes later. This is on purpose: giving old tickets targets counted from the day they were opened would mark all of them as breached at once. The clock runs 24 hours a day; office hours and holidays are not taken into account.');
$add('MAIL-010', 'Email to ticket', 'Reading a message', 'pass', 'Encoded senders and subjects, quoted-printable and base64 text, other character sets, messages with several parts (the plain text is used, attachments are skipped) and HTML-only mail (tags, scripts and styles removed) are read correctly. The quoted earlier mail is cut off a reply, in English and Dutch. Out-of-office answers, bulk mail, mailing lists and bounces are recognised as automatic.');
$add('MAIL-011', 'Email to ticket', 'From message to ticket or reply', 'pass', 'A new message opens a ticket linked to the known person and company, with SLA targets, and the sender gets one confirmation with the reference. A reply with the reference in the subject, or one that answers a known mail, is added to the thread without the quoted text; it reopens a resolved ticket and ends "Waiting". A stranger who quotes a reference gets a new ticket instead. The same message twice, automatic mail, mail from our own addresses and a message without a sender open nothing, and one sender can open at most ten tickets an hour. HTML in a message is shown as text, never run.');
$add('MAIL-012', 'Email to ticket', 'The mailbox, the settings and replying', 'pass', 'Against a stand-in IMAP server: the connection test counts unread mail without reading it; a wrong password, a missing folder and a closed port are each reported, and the error never holds the password. One run turned three messages into one ticket, one reply and one ignored message and marked all three as read; a second run found nothing, and messages offered again were recognised. The mailbox password is stored encrypted and never shown; a blank password keeps the saved one. A reply ticked "also email" is mailed to the customer with the reference and a sign-off; a comment without the tick is not.');
$add('MAIL-013', 'Email to ticket', 'Not tried against a real mailbox', 'open', 'The IMAP reader is written in-house and could only be tried against a stand-in server written from the same understanding of the protocol. Before relying on it, save the real mailbox under Settings > Tickets and use "Test the connection". Attachments are not stored, and only the first 512 KB of a message is read. Under Privacy requests the tickets and replies a sender mailed in are part of the lookup and the export, and the address can be removed from them, also for a sender without a user account; what the person wrote inside a ticket stays and has to be checked by hand.');

$add('CONN-006', 'Connectors', '3CX: a system administrator\'s own login', 'fixed', 'The owner reported "the service rejected the credentials" when connecting 3CX with system administrator credentials. The connector only signed in as an API client (client ID and secret), which a normal admin user name and password are not, so a valid login was refused. The message also hid why.', 'The connector now tries the API client first and then the same two values as a Management Console login. A refusal says which of the two failed, shows the OAuth error code the PBX gave (for example invalid_client) and explains the two-step sign-in case. Tested against a stand-in 3CX for all four cases; a real 3CX with two-step sign-in or an unusual login flow has not been tried.');
$add('CONN-007', 'Connectors', 'A log under each connector', 'pass', 'Every test and sync is written to a log under the connector with its result, the message and one line per request: address and path, HTTP code, the error code the service gave (for example invalid_client) and, when there was no answer, the connection error. Checked through the real settings page against a stand-in 3CX: a refusal, a good test, a PBX that does not answer and an address that is refused before any request. The log never holds the secret, keeps the newest 40 entries per service, is purged after 90 days and opens by itself after a failure. A scheduled sync is only written down when its result changes.');
$add('CONN-008', 'Connectors', '3CX: signed in but not allowed to read call history', 'fixed', 'With the new log the owner showed what 3CX answered: the token request got HTTP 200 (the Client ID and secret were right) and the call-history request got HTTP 403. The program reported both as "the service rejected the credentials", which sent the owner looking at the credentials while the real cause was the permissions of the API client in 3CX.', 'An HTTP 403 on a data request made with a token that was just accepted is now its own result, "Signed in, but not allowed", with an explanation for 3CX (the API client must be allowed to use the Configuration API and have a role that may read call reports). A refusal of the credentials themselves is still "Unauthorized". Checked against a stand-in 3CX; the exact 3CX permission that fixes it for the owner is to be confirmed on their PBX.');
$add('CONN-009', 'Connectors', '3CX: the call history is slow to answer', 'fixed', 'After the permissions were fixed the log showed the token request at HTTP 200 and the call-history request ending in "no answer: Operation timed out after 10012 milliseconds" (curl error 28). The question was unfiltered and the wait was 10 seconds, and the message said the service "did not answer in time, or refused the connection" although it had just signed the program in.', 'The test now asks only for the last day, newest first, and waits up to 30 seconds (the sync waits 30 seconds per request and asks for the last 35 days, newest first); the web page lifts its own 30 second limit for it. A timeout after a successful sign-in now says so: signed in, the credentials and permissions are right, 3CX is slow with a large history. Checked against a stand-in 3CX that answers after 3 seconds: a 1 second wait reports the timeout, an 8 second wait connects. Not yet confirmed on the owner\'s PBX: if /xapi/v1/CallHistoryView is still too slow there, the log will show it.');
$add('CONN-010', 'Connectors', '3CX: the call history answers HTTP 500, or hangs', 'fixed', 'The log of the owner showed the sign-in at HTTP 200 and then the call-history list answering HTTP 500 with nothing in it as soon as it was filtered on StartTime, and hanging for 30 seconds without a filter (the PBX has a large history and tried to return all of it).', 'The call history is now asked for through the call-log function of the 3CX reports (ReportCallLogData, Pbx.GetCallLogData) with a start and end date, first with and then without sorting, and only then through the CallHistoryView list with a start date. Every form is limited to a period: the program never asks for the whole history again. A form is only skipped after a refused question (HTTP 400, 404 or 500). The log shows 3CX\'s own error text, the fields of the first record that came back, and, when nothing works, which call-log views and fields the PBX offers. Durations in the form 3CX writes them (seconds, hh:mm:ss, d.hh:mm:ss, ISO 8601) are read. Checked against a stand-in that behaves like the log of the owner; not yet confirmed on the real PBX, and the field names of the call-log function are from documentation: the first record in the log will show whether they match.');

return ['version' => 31, 'entries' => $e];
